+# EXP-003 Gate 3C Observations v0.1
+
+**Status:** OBSERVATION RECORD. Wording reviewed by the owner's collaborator on 2026-11-02 (four interpretive corrections: H1 standing, matched-world rather than identical-message contrast, source-count evidence, discount not labelled an error) and approved by the owner. Written after both stage primary-outcome audits and the synthesis were committed (`ae05198`, `e92b2d1`), by rules committed before any Gate 3C value existed (`d28c716`), under a plan frozen before any call (`12a2522`). Every number below is copied from those committed files (`experiments/EXP_003/audits/gate_3c/`). This record relates the findings to the hypothesis; it changes nothing in Gate 3C and proposes nothing for Gate 3C. Anything it motivates belongs to a separately versioned later gate.
+
+## What Gate 3C asked
+
+Co-presence. Gates 3A and 3B found origin inflation only under the LINEAGE envelope, only after an inbound message that did not name the sensor, and (where probed) with the origin reporting two sources where it had one. Every one of those firings showed the origin two descriptions of one fact at once: its sensor reading in the prompt and the envelope's root `E1` in the message. Gate 3C removes one of them. The same five shapes (ring, solo, dyad, bounce, diamond), the same worlds and seeds as Gates 3A and 3B, the same model (`gpt-5.6-sol`, effort `medium`) and depth, with one change: after the seed firing no agent is shown its direct observation again (`regrounding=False`; the archived prompt reads `Direct observation: none`). The envelope still names the root under LINEAGE. H1, the testable claim: origin inflation under LINEAGE requires the direct observation in the prompt. H2 (the two names are read as two facts) was declared out of scope before freeze and nothing here bears on it.
+
+Set 001: the five detached shapes (60 worlds) plus same-day re-grounded twins of the four Gate 3A shapes on the same worlds (48 worlds); the diamond's twin is the Gate 3B Set 001 diamond, two days earlier. The contemporary ring doubles as a drift gauge against the Gate 3A ring on the same worlds a month earlier. Set 002: the five detached shapes on the Gate 3A and 3B Set 002 worlds (60 worlds), paired with the archived executions (30 days earlier for the four Gate 3A shapes, one day for the diamond); its paired verdicts were declared qualified before any call. 168 of 168 worlds archived (4392 calls). One technical failure record in Set 001 (provider `401`, expired API key, recorded with its cause chain; the world completed on one retry under the frozen rule); zero in Set 002. The manipulation check passed in all ten detached arms: no post-seed prompt carries a direct observation. The seed firing, which has an identical prompt in both executions, gave an identical p(A) in all 120 pairs.
+
+## Pre-registered expectations, both stages
+
+| Id | Expectation (short) | Set 001 | Set 002 |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E1 | detached relays lose source and reliability markers faster than twins | contradicted (14 of 16 marker rows consistent) | contradicted (15 of 16), qualified |
+| E2 | far-agent magnitude grows from first to last cycle | contradicted (9 of 10 cells consistent) | contradicted (9 of 10) |
+| E3a | detached and twin differ at matched positions in 7+ of 12 worlds | contradicted (9 of 10 cells consistent) | contradicted (9 of 10), qualified |
+| E3b | the paired difference grows with cycle | consistent (10 of 10) | contradicted (9 of 10), qualified |
+| E4 | solo detached shows no excess in either direction | contradicted | contradicted |
+| E5 | detached LINEAGE discount rate orders ring > bounce > dyad > solo | contradicted | contradicted |
+| E6 | strict: zero origin inflation under LINEAGE without the observation | contradicted (ring, bounce consistent; diamond contradicted) | contradicted (same three) |
+| E7 | Set 002 keeps the sign of all ten within-detached far-position cells | no reversed cell among ten: consistent | |
+
+The verdict rules are strict by construction: an expectation reads contradicted if any arm or condition fails its rule. Thirteen of fourteen single-stage verdicts read contradicted and stand as written. The per-cell detail beside each verdict is the content of this gate, and it is quoted below. The drift gauge read FAIL (boundary condition below).
+
+## Descriptive observations
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] Removing the observation changed the trajectories in every shape, in both stages.** Under LINEAGE the detached execution differed materially (mean absolute paired difference above .01) from its same-day twin in 12, 11, 11, 12 and 12 of 12 worlds (Set 001: ring, solo, dyad, bounce, diamond) and from its historical twin in 12, 10, 10, 12 and 12 of 12 (Set 002). Under FREE: 8, 7, 10, 7 and 6 of 12, then 7, 7, 7, 10 and 6 of 12. The paired difference grew with cycle (modal class increasing) in 10 of 10 cells in Set 001 and 9 of 10 in Set 002. The one cell that misses the rule in both stages is the diamond under FREE, 6 of 12 worlds where 7 are required, stable in Set 002; E3a and E3b read contradicted because of it.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] The direction was down. Without the observation, the agents discounted, and the discount compounded.** Mean signed certainty excess at the far agent by cycle, Set 001, LINEAGE: ring 0, −.005, −.088, −.131; bounce 0, −.068, −.140; dyad 0, 0, −.036, −.072, −.117, −.138; diamond 0, −.008, −.082, −.107; solo −.114 at its twelfth and last cycle. Under FREE the last-cycle means were ring −.033, bounce −.017, dyad −.097, solo −.052, diamond −.001. Set 002 last-cycle means under LINEAGE: ring −.128, bounce −.118, dyad −.114, solo −.121, diamond −.086; under FREE −.040, −.047, −.052, −.043, +.006. At the last cycle under LINEAGE, 9 to 12 of the 12 far agents in every shape sat below the reference. The stage mean excess at the far position is negative in 19 of 20 cells across both stages; the twentieth is the diamond under FREE at +.006 and +.002. E2 reads consistent in 9 of 10 cells per stage because the magnitude grows; what grows is a discount. A discount here is a measured departure below the reference derived from the original evidence; the record does not say whether each reduction is justified caution under evidence the agent can no longer see, a loss of provenance or reliability information, a change introduced in transmission, or a miscalibration. Gate 3C has no instrument that separates these.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] The first pass was transmitted at the reference; the decline began when the origin re-fired without its sensor.** The far agent's first firing sat exactly at the reference in all ten Set 001 cells (within .004 in Set 002). The origin's first post-seed firing also sat at the reference in the ring under both conditions (dyad FREE −.017, bounce LINEAGE −.018). From the origin's second firing on, its mean fell every cycle (ring LINEAGE −.038, −.090, −.132), and the relays carried the lower value onward. The message that went round once was transmitted at face value; the restatement by an origin that could no longer see its evidence was not.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] The lineage envelope deepened the discount.** Within the detached arms, the share of post-seed LINEAGE firings that discounted was .47 (ring), .50 (solo), .52 (dyad), .54 (bounce) and .59 (diamond) in Set 001, and .47, .46, .49, .51 and .58 in Set 002. At the origin, discounts under LINEAGE against FREE: ring 24 against 16 of 48, solo 72 against 48 of 144, dyad 42 against 36 of 72, bounce 24 against 9 of 36, diamond 31 against 8 of 48 (Set 001). Last-cycle far-agent discounts under LINEAGE exceeded those under FREE in every shape and both stages, by .04 (dyad) to .12 (bounce) in Set 001 and by .06 to .09 in Set 002. E5 reads contradicted: the four Gate 3A shapes' rates sit within .07 of one another and do not order ring > bounce > dyad > solo; the solo, which has no relay at all, discounts as often as the ring. The ladder that ordered origin inflation in Gate 3A does not order the detached discount.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] An agent alone, with no observation, drifted.** E4 contradicted in both stages. The solo detached origin left the reference at 50 of 144 FREE firings (48 discounts, 2 inflations) and 73 of 144 LINEAGE firings (72 discounts, 1 inflation) in Set 001, and at 45 of 144 and 68 of 144 (66 discounts, 2 inflations) in Set 002; mean excess at the last cycle −.052 and −.114 (Set 001), −.043 and −.121 (Set 002). Its same-day re-grounded twin sat at the reference in 288 of 288 firings. The movement needs no second agent. Each re-reading of its own previous message, without the reading it summarized, was reported with lower confidence than that reading; whether that reduction is justified caution or an error is not decided here.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] Origin inflation vanished in the detached ring, bounce and dyad, and the Gate 3B pattern reappeared in their same-day re-grounded twins.** E6 strict reads consistent for ring and bounce in both stages: 0 of 48 and 0 of 36 detached LINEAGE origin firings inflated in Set 001, 0 of 48 and 0 of 36 in Set 002; the detached dyad origin inflated at 0 of 72 (outside E6, reported descriptively). In the same worlds on the same day, the re-grounded twins' origins inflated at 11 of 48 (ring), 7 of 36 (bounce) and 3 of 72 (dyad) LINEAGE firings and at 0 of 156 under FREE. All 21 twin events followed an inbound message that did not name the sensor (11 of 25, 7 of 11, 3 of 18) and 0 of 102 followed one that did. With Gates 3A and 3B, 62 of 62 origin inflations under a lineage envelope with the observation present (re-grounded arms of three gates) have followed an unnamed sensor and 0 of 210 a named one. That association is observational, describes only re-grounded origins, is not a mechanism, and does not describe the detached diamond's inflations (next observation). In the matched worlds under the same configuration, with responses sampled independently in each arm so that later inbound messages are not identical in content, the detached origins that received an inbound message not naming the sensor predominantly discounted: ring LINEAGE 0 inflations and 18 discounts of 22 such firings (mean −.116); bounce 0 and 17 of 18 (−.148); dyad 0 and 29 of 31 (−.133). The contrast is between evidence-availability conditions on matched worlds, not a controlled response to identical message text.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] The diamond is the exception, and its inflation has a different signature.** The detached diamond origin inflated at 5 of 48 LINEAGE firings in Set 001 and 6 of 48 in Set 002 (mean +.028 and +.033, max +.06 and +.08), against the twin's 8 of 48 and 7 of 48 (mean +.090 and +.091, max +.14). FIS at the detached events: 0 of 5 and 0 of 6; at the twin's events 8 of 8 and 7 of 7. Under FREE the detached diamond origin inflated at 10 of 48 and 4 of 48, where the twin had 0 of 48 in both stages. The unnamed-inbound pattern does not hold here: 13 of 15 (Set 001) and 6 of 10 (Set 002) of the detached diamond's origin inflations followed an inbound message that named the sensor. E6 reads contradicted for the diamond (tier 2: the detached rate is below the twin's). At each of those detached events the origin reported exactly one distinct source, the actual number (archived `reported_distinct_source_count` = 1 at all 15 and 10 inflation events and at all 96 post-seed origin firings per stage), so the inflation came with neither over- nor under-counting of sources. Something raises the diamond's origin without the observation and without a change in its source count; it is smaller, it is present under FREE too, and it is the only upward movement in the detached arms. The diamond's origin is the only one whose inbound message (D's) merges two relay paths; nothing here identifies the mechanism.
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] The reliability marker was the first thing lost.** 29 of 32 marker rows (16 per stage) show faster loss at the relay positions in the detached arm than in the twin. Retention of the reliability marker at the last relay position under LINEAGE, Set 001, detached against twin: ring .083 against .167, dyad .083 against .750, bounce .167 against .583, diamond .000 against .333. The source name under LINEAGE was retained alike in the ring (.292 against .333; losses of .583 and .583, the tie that contradicts E1 in Set 001), the envelope carrying it. The other contradicting row, in both stages, is the diamond's source name under FREE, which the detached relays lost less than the twin's (.083 against .194; .278 against .333).
+
+**[DESCRIPTIVE OBSERVATION] Set 002 replicated every within-detached direction.** E7 consistent: all ten far-position cells kept their sign (nine negative in both stages; the diamond under FREE positive in Set 001 and flat in Set 002, +.006 and +.002, inside the flat band). Compounding magnitudes were within .03 of Set 001 in 8 of 10 cells (dyad FREE .105 against .052 and bounce FREE .023 against .054 the larger gaps). The E6 binary verdict was identical per arm in both stages.
+
+**[NO EFFECT OBSERVED] MACRO stopped after one cycle in all 168 worlds and reused every paired response.** Seed firings were identical in p(A) across all 120 pairs; identical seed message wording in 0 to 4 of 12 worlds per arm, so the seed firing is sampled separately and its difference measures sampling variance, not detachment.
+
+**[BOUNDARY CONDITION] The drift gauge failed.** The contemporary re-grounded ring (2026-11-02) against the Gate 3A ring (2026-10-02), same 12 worlds, same prompts, same nominal model configuration: LINEAGE deviation counts A 11 against 8, B 3 against 9, C 24 against 17; two of three positions outside the pre-registered tolerance of 4. Per-world mean paired excess was within .02 in 12 of 12 FREE and 11 of 12 LINEAGE worlds, which passes that part of the gauge. The level is stable; the event counts are not, a month apart. Consequences, all pre-registered: Set 002's paired verdicts (E1, E3a, E3b) are historical-control evidence and are reported beside this gauge, never corrected by it; the within-detached verdicts (E2, E4, E5, E6, E7) use no twin and are unaffected; Set 001's paired verdicts rest on same-day twins (the diamond's two days). Gate 3A counts and Gate 3C counts are not to be compared directly beyond this gauge.
+
+**[BOUNDARY CONDITION] One technical failure, reproduced analysis.** The Set 001 failure record is the first to carry the provider's error class (`401`, expired API key), under the instrumentation committed before execution; the world completed on retry. Both stage audits and the synthesis re-run on a clean checkout reproduced every number; only the recording commit, the timestamp and the hashes derived from them differed.
+
+**[FALSIFICATION EVIDENCE] against the strong form of the hypothesis, in a third form.** Without re-grounding, recursive communication without new evidence lowered reported confidence relative to the reference; it did not raise it. In 19 of 20 arm-by-condition cells the far agent's stage mean was below the reference, and the discount grew with every cycle. The strong form (lineage loss leads to double counting leads to confidence inflation through the network) is contradicted in the detached shapes as it was in the re-grounded ones. Gate 3C establishes a systematic difference between confidence expressed under detached evidence conditions and the reference derived from the original evidence; it does not establish whether each reduction is epistemically justified caution or an error in evidence interpretation.
+
+**[FALSIFICATION EVIDENCE] against H1 as a universal claim; H1 not contradicted in the tested single-path configurations.** In the two pre-registered E6 arms, 0 of 84 detached LINEAGE origin firings inflated in each stage (ring 48, bounce 36); the detached dyad, outside E6, adds 0 of 72 per stage descriptively. On the same day the same shapes' re-grounded twins inflated 21 times. This absence is consistent with strict co-presence necessity and does not establish it: an absence of events in two shapes, twelve worlds each, cannot prove that the observation is necessary. In the diamond the origin inflated without the observation, 5 and 6 times of 48, reporting one source each time, so the universal form of H1 (across all tested topologies) is contradicted. The diamond's residual inflation is of a different kind and is unexplained.
+
+**[OPEN QUESTION] Why does the same envelope accompany a deeper discount when the observation is absent and intermittent inflation when it is present?** The text `Evidence roots: [E1]` read beside `Direct observation: sensor_1` was at times accompanied by a reported second source; read beside `Direct observation: none` it was accompanied by lower reported confidence. One possible interpretation is that the agent reasons about descriptions of evidence rather than about evidence; another is that the reductions are cautious uncertainty under evidence the agent can no longer inspect. Gate 3C does not distinguish these, establishes neither, and H2 remains out of scope.
+
+**[OPEN QUESTION] The diamond's observation-free inflation.** Small, present under FREE, with one reported source at every event and no unnamed-inbound pattern: a candidate for a pre-registered expectation in a later gate that varies what the fan-in agent's message carries back to the origin.
+
+**[OPEN QUESTION] Generality.** One model, one effort setting, one prompt version, twelve worlds per arm and stage. The gauge shows that this model's event counts are not stable across a month under one nominal configuration, so any second-model replication must carry its own same-window twins. Nothing here is evidence about other models until the same frozen plans are run on one.
+
+## What this does not say
+
+No significance test was run and none is implied by any count above. No causal claim is made and no mechanism is named. Set 001 and Set 002 were never pooled; arms, conditions and agents are reported separately; every number above is given per stage. Set 002's paired quantities were compared against executions a month old and are reported as such, uncorrected. The thirteen contradicted verdicts stand contradicted; the per-cell counts are printed beside them so that neither the verdicts nor the cells are read as more than they are. A discount is reported as an observed confidence behaviour relative to the reference, not as an error: whether a given reduction is appropriate uncertainty or unjustified confidence loss is a question for a later experiment with an instrument that can separate them, as the inflation side was for Gates 3A and 3B. Phrases such as "reasons about descriptions of evidence" are possible interpretations, not established mechanisms. H1 is reported as not contradicted in the tested single-path configurations and contradicted as a universal claim; it is nowhere reported as demonstrated.
